      "id": "spf:scrum-method",
      "type": [
        "schema:HowTo",
        "spf:Methodology",
        "skos:Concept"
      ],
      "Agile Method Name": "Scrum Method",
      "Data Type": [
        {
          "id": "spf:methodology",
          "label": "Methodology"
        }
      ],
      "Method Splash Image": [
        {
          "name": "scrum-framework-with-sdo-logo-9.29.23.png",
          "url": "https://baserow-backend-production20240528124524339000000001.s3.amazonaws.com/user_files/ae4ENBPWwpMjLxbtDGEdL1pYsZnZDaJn_468ddcf35156ee7a5627e7ffdc97b3e4a657544bb1af593c1ae150e989eeffe5.png"
        }
      ],
      "When Is This Method Used?": "Scrum fits when you are building something complex that keeps changing, and the team needs a steady rhythm to stay on top of it. It helps most when regular feedback and quick course-correction matter, and when clear roles and a predictable cadence keep everyone moving in the same direction. If a team does better with routine than with a free-for-all, Scrum gives it that shape.",
      "Resource to Learn More": "https://www.scrum.org/resources/what-scrum-module",
