      ],
      "When Is This Method Used?": "Kanban is the method to reach for when work arrives as a steady stream, like support, operations, or maintenance, and you want to improve how it flows without tearing up the way you already work. It suits teams whose priorities shift often and who value flexibility over fixed cycles. Because you can lay it on top of an existing process, it is often an easy first step into agile.",
