        }
      ],
      "When Is This Method Used?": "Use Continuous Discovery when you want to stay close to your users and let what you learn shape the product as you go. It is most useful when user needs are unclear or keep changing, and when the team would rather adjust based on real evidence than commit to a fixed plan up front. It fits teams that treat learning as a constant habit, not a one-time phase.",
      "Resource to Learn More": "https://www.interaction-design.org/literature/topics/continuous-discovery",
