      ],
      "Who Created This Method?": "Continuous Discovery was shaped and popularized by product coach Teresa Torres in her 2021 book, Continuous Discovery Habits. It builds on lean and agile ideas about learning from customers often. Official source: producttalk.org.",
      "How Does This Method Compare to to Other Agile Methods?": "Continuous Discovery is not a delivery method like Scrum or Kanban. It focuses on deciding what to build, while Scrum and Kanban focus on building it, so teams usually run it alongside one of them. It shares the test-and-learn mindset of Lean UX, but as an ongoing weekly habit rather than a project-by-project cycle.",
      "During While Kinds of Work Environments Is It Best to Use This Method?": "It fits product teams that can reach customers regularly and that work toward an outcome rather than a fixed feature list. It is best where user needs change or are not fully understood, and where a cross-functional trio can share the discovery work.",
      "Steps to Perform the Method": "Continuous Discovery is a set of weekly habits:\n1. Talk to at least one customer every week as a full product trio (product, design, and engineering).\n2. Map what you learn on an opportunity solution tree that connects customer needs to a clear outcome.\n3. Surface and test your assumptions before building anything.\n4. Run small experiments to check ideas quickly.\n5. Keep repeating so learning never stops."
    },
