      "Method Splash Image": [
        {
          "name": "lean_ux.gif",
          "url": "https://baserow-backend-production20240528124524339000000001.s3.amazonaws.com/user_files/48YLCucYztxPTGMspkKQKD0M0zh1FZ7D_f7de92dfd7201bcd5549a7d36673011b2899d7c69df2459eb5c88012b9c86f60.gif"
        }
      ],
      "When Is This Method Used?": "Lean UX is the right call when you are building something user-centered and are open to changing course based on what you learn. It helps most early on, when the real need is still fuzzy and the team wants to test ideas quickly instead of building a lot on a guess. It suits groups that value working closely together over producing polished documents.",
      "Resource to Learn More": "https://www.interaction-design.org/literature/article/a-simple-introduction-to-lean-ux",
